# Git Workflow — Direct Push to main

This project uses **direct push to `main`**. Do not create pull requests unless the user explicitly asks.

## Default branch

- Work on **`main`** only.
- Before pushing: `git pull origin main` (merge/rebase as needed).
- Push with: `git push origin main`

## When the user asks to commit or push

1. Confirm changes on `main` (`git status`, `git branch`).
2. If not on `main`, checkout `main` and merge/rebase local work first.
3. Commit on `main` when explicitly requested.
4. Push to **`origin main`** — not feature branches, not PR flow.

## Do not

- Run `gh pr create` or suggest opening a PR by default.
- Push to `cursor/*` or other long-lived feature branches unless the user asks.
- Force-push `main` unless the user explicitly requests it.

## If push is rejected (non-fast-forward)

1. `git pull origin main` to integrate remote changes.
2. Resolve conflicts if any, commit, then `git push origin main`.
